Scrape availability|up{job="api"}|A PromQL selector returns the latest scrape-success signal for matching targets.|Check whether the collector can currently retrieve target metrics.|1 means a successful scrape and 0 a failed scrape; missing targets may produce no series.|{instance="host:9090",job="api"} 1|PromQL query, not shell. Scrape health is not application health.
Counter rate|rate(http_requests_total{job="api"}[5m])|Calculates a reset-aware per-second rate for each counter series.|Turn a cumulative request counter into recent throughput.|Each result retains source labels; apply rate before aggregating different instances.|{instance="a",status="200"} 12.5|Illustrative metric; use a window with enough samples for the scrape interval.
Aggregated throughput|sum by (job) (rate(http_requests_total[5m]))|Aggregates per-series request rates by service job.|Compare service traffic without averaging raw counters.|One output series per job shows requests per second across instances.|{job="api"} 125|PromQL; label names and counting semantics must match instrumentation.
Error ratio|sum(rate(http_requests_total{job="api",status=~"5.."}[5m])) / sum(rate(http_requests_total{job="api"}[5m]))|Computes a ratio of server-error requests to total requests.|Monitor a defined failure population alongside traffic.|0.02 means 2% under this definition; absent traffic requires separate interpretation.|0.02|PromQL example; 5xx-only may omit business failures or client-visible timeouts.
Classic histogram p95|histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(http_request_duration_seconds_bucket{job="api"}[5m])))|Estimates p95 latency from cumulative classic histogram buckets.|Inspect the slow tail across instances.|Result is seconds; le must remain in aggregation and bucket layout limits precision.|0.25|PromQL for classic histograms; native histogram syntax and semantics differ.
Mean latency|sum(rate(http_request_duration_seconds_sum{job="api"}[5m])) / sum(rate(http_request_duration_seconds_count{job="api"}[5m]))|Divides observed duration accumulation by observation count.|Compare mean latency with tail behavior.|The unit is seconds per observation; a healthy mean can coexist with a bad p99.|0.08|PromQL; requires matching sum/count series and a nonempty population.
Absent target signal|absent(up{job="api"})|Returns a signal when no matching series exists.|Detect disappearance from discovery rather than only failed scrapes.|A returned 1 means the selector has no series; an empty result means at least one match exists.|{job="api"} 1|PromQL; use expected-target inventory for per-instance absence rather than this service-wide check alone.
Counter resets|resets(http_requests_total{job="api"}[1h])|Counts observed decreases in a counter over one hour.|Correlate rate changes with restarts or instrumentation resets.|A positive result identifies resets within that series; replacement labels can instead create a new series.|{instance="a"} 2|PromQL; resets are not automatically application failures.
Configuration validation|promtool check config prometheus.yml|Validates Prometheus configuration and referenced rule files.|Catch invalid configuration before a controlled reload.|SUCCESS indicates accepted syntax and referenced-file checks, not target reachability.|SUCCESS: prometheus.yml is valid prometheus config file syntax|Local validation; use a trusted configuration and installed promtool matching deployment expectations.
Rule validation|promtool check rules alerts.yml|Checks recording and alerting rule syntax.|Find invalid expressions before publishing rules.|Read file and rule errors; a valid expression can still measure the wrong population.|SUCCESS: ... rules found|Local read-only validation; add rule tests for behavioral expectations.
Rule unit tests|promtool test rules tests.yml|Runs rule tests against supplied input series and expected results.|Verify alert timing and query behavior under resets, gaps and failures.|PASS means the specified cases matched; untested scenarios remain unknown.|SUCCESS|Runs local test definitions; fixtures should include missing data and recovery.
Metrics endpoint sample|curl -fsS --max-time 5 http://127.0.0.1:9090/metrics|Retrieves a local Prometheus-format metrics endpoint.|Check that exposition exists and inspect metric names and labels.|HELP and TYPE describe metric families; sample labels define individual series.|# TYPE prometheus_build_info gauge|Read-only HTTP request; endpoint and port are examples and output may expose infrastructure metadata.
